# SkyRoute email settings.
#
# 1) Copy this file to a new file named  .env  (same folder as main.py).
# 2) Fill in your own values.  The .env file is in .gitignore, so it is never uploaded to GitHub.
# 3) Without a .env file the program still works: emails are saved as text files in data/outbox/.
#
# ---- Example: Gmail ----
# Gmail does not accept your normal password here. Turn on 2-Step Verification, then create an
# "App password" at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords and paste it below (spaces are fine).
SKYROUTE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SKYROUTE_SMTP_PORT=465
SKYROUTE_SMTP_USER=your.name@gmail.com
SKYROUTE_SMTP_PASSWORD=your-16-letter-app-password

# Optional. The sender address shown in the email (defaults to SKYROUTE_SMTP_USER).
# SKYROUTE_MAIL_FROM=your.name@gmail.com

# Optional. ssl (port 465), starttls (port 587) or none. Chosen from the port when left out.
# SKYROUTE_SMTP_SECURITY=ssl

# After filling this file in, check it with:  python main.py --test-email your_address@gmail.com

# Optional. The key that encrypts data/users.json. When left out, a key is created automatically
# in data/secret.key (never uploaded). Keep a copy: without the key the users file cannot be read.
# Make one with:  python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
# SKYROUTE_DATA_KEY=
